# Teensy default build — capture-serial

## Default environment

For **firmware** build and upload, use **`teensy41-capture-serial`** (not plain `teensy41`) unless the user explicitly requests another env in this session.

```bash
pio run -e teensy41-capture-serial
pio run -e teensy41-capture-serial -t upload
```

This env enables `SESSION_CAPTURE` and `PERF_TELEMETRY` so USB serial emits `#CAP`, `REVT`, `ST`, and edit/transition lines needed for HITL verification and capture sessions.

## When the user opts out

Use a different env only when they clearly ask, for example:

- "plain teensy41" / "production build" / "no serial capture"
- `teensy41-capture` (CAP lines without full serial telemetry)
- `teensy41-capture-bypass` (diagnostic bypass)
- compile-check only with a named env

If unclear, default to **`teensy41-capture-serial`**.

## When this rule does **not** apply

- **Host tests:** `pio test -e native` (unchanged)
- **On-device PlatformIO tests:** use the env the user names (`teensy41`, etc.)
- User says **not to build or upload** in this session

## After build

Follow [Teensy-Upload-After-Build.mdc](Teensy-Upload-After-Build.mdc): ask before upload; reuse the same env for upload.

